1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,347
Could a yeti really survive in

2
00:00:01,347 --> 00:00:02,344
the Himalayas?

3
00:00:03,100 --> 00:00:04,051
Let's build one.

4
00:00:04,563 --> 00:00:06,246
In Sherpa and Tibetan stories,

5
00:00:06,246 --> 00:00:06,966
it's a huge,

6
00:00:06,966 --> 00:00:08,846
hairy walker of the high snow.

7
00:00:09,276 --> 00:00:10,937
But a big body sinks in

8
00:00:10,937 --> 00:00:11,783
deep snow.

9
00:00:11,796 --> 00:00:12,852
So you grow wide,

10
00:00:12,852 --> 00:00:13,780
furry feet,

11
00:00:13,793 --> 00:00:15,045
like a snowshoe hare.

12
00:00:15,209 --> 00:00:16,440
They spread your weight,

13
00:00:16,440 --> 00:00:17,646
so you stay on top.

14
00:00:17,810 --> 00:00:18,762
But the air up here is

15
00:00:18,762 --> 00:00:19,295
thin.

16
00:00:19,342 --> 00:00:20,480
So you tune your body for

17
00:00:20,480 --> 00:00:21,397
low oxygen,

18
00:00:21,397 --> 00:00:22,337
like the yak,

19
00:00:22,419 --> 00:00:23,707
whose genes are built for high

20
00:00:23,707 --> 00:00:24,461
altitude.

21
00:00:24,729 --> 00:00:25,925
But then winter comes,

22
00:00:25,925 --> 00:00:27,259
and there's nothing to eat.

23
00:00:27,690 --> 00:00:28,965
So you sleep through it,

24
00:00:29,013 --> 00:00:30,151
like a brown bear,

25
00:00:30,151 --> 00:00:32,030
living on stored fat for months.

26
00:00:32,937 --> 00:00:34,376
Now look at what you built.

27
00:00:34,539 --> 00:00:35,073
A big,

28
00:00:35,073 --> 00:00:36,024
furry bear.

29
00:00:36,455 --> 00:00:37,893
In twenty seventeen,

30
00:00:37,941 --> 00:00:40,250
scientists tested nine yeti samples.

31
00:00:40,588 --> 00:00:41,760
One was a dog.

32
00:00:42,028 --> 00:00:43,838
The other eight were Asian bears.

33
00:00:44,349 --> 00:00:45,743
And the name yeti comes from

34
00:00:45,743 --> 00:00:47,588
Tibetan words meaning rock bear.

35
00:00:47,926 --> 00:00:49,399
So the legend isn't empty.

36
00:00:49,516 --> 00:00:51,233
It grew from a real animal.

